    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\ntabline\n\n### Description\n\nHello. I wish for tabline to not show itself when I have only 1 file open. Is this possible? Not a big deal. I just don't like the way it looks, especially when using nvim as a manpager.\r\n\r\nThanks!\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0-dev (nightly)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nJust using basic config.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nDo no show when only 1 file open.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nTabline is open (especially during nvim as manpager).",
